<p:notes xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Slide Image Placeholder 1"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1" noRot="1" noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldImg"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Notes Placeholder 2"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>SOURCE KEY</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>A: https://</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>huggingface.co</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>/Qwen/Qwen3-8B-GGUF/tree/main (chosen weight file and size).</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>B: https://</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>huggingface.co</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>/Qwen/Qwen3-8B (original model card); https://</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>huggingface.co</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>/Qwen/Qwen3-8B/blob/main/</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>config.json</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t> (architecture).</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>Cache setting: assumed 16-bit values, 2 bytes each. This is independent of the chosen Q4_K_M weights.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>All arithmetic results are calculated estimates, not measured peak memory.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>DELIVERY</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>Use after the Hugging Face screenshot. Click to reveal the calculations.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>SPEAKER NARRATION</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>Each learned weight needs storage. Eight bits make a byte. Multiply the number of weights by bits per weight and divide by eight to estimate bytes. With the rounded 8.2 billion parameter count, eight bits per weight gives 8.2 billion bytes, or 8.2 decimal GB. Five bits gives 5.125 GB, rounded to 5.13 GB, and four bits gives 4.1 GB. These are ideal weight payload calculations. They are useful for understanding the relationship without teaching floating-point format names. Actual quantized files also contain scales, metadata, and some values at different precisions. That is why the chosen Q4_K_M file is 5.03 GB rather than the ideal 4.1 GB and Q8_0 is 8.71 GB rather than 8.2 GB. The Q5_K_M file is 5.85 GB rather than the ideal 5.13 GB. Quantization retains the parameter count while changing the numerical representation, and may change quality or performance. Use the actual selected file as the next budgeting input when the engine keeps that compressed representation in memory. The file size is still an estimate of loaded weight storage, not a measurement of peak inference memory. Runtime conversion can change it. The slide uses decimal GB throughout.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>SOURCES</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>https://</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>huggingface.co</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>/Qwen/Qwen3-8B-GGUF/tree/main</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Slide Number Placeholder 3"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldNum" idx="5"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" marR="0" lvl="0" indent="0" algn="l" defTabSz="914400" rtl="0"